#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Slack, as an agent is reached on it.

Everything about this platform is in this file and nowhere else (R-CAD-13). A channel id, a
`ts`, a `thread_ts`, a Socket Mode envelope, the four-thousand-character message limit and
the three seconds a slash command has to be acknowledged in are all Slack's, and none of
them appears outside this program. Nothing here is imported by Rundesk, and nothing here
imports Rundesk.

What it does, in the order somebody experiences it:

    named in a channel -> the turn happens in a thread under it   (R-SLK-1)
    inside that thread -> it answers without being named again    (R-SLK-3)
    in a direct message -> it answers where it was spoken to      (R-SLK-4)
    taken up -> 👀            finished -> ✅ and the answer, whole
    stopped  -> ✋            failed   -> ⚠️ and what failed

The contract this implements is
`docs/extending/channel-adapters/references/the-contract.md`. Where the two disagree, the
reference is right. `.knowledge/prd/channel-slack.md` is what it is held to.

**Where this is deliberately not Discord.** Slack has no generic typing indicator for a
bot — `assistant.threads.setStatus` exists but requires the Agents/AI Apps feature and
forces a thread-only UI on every conversation — so a turn says it is working through the
👀 mark and the running commentary, and there is no indicator to renew. Presence is not
set here either: `users.setPresence` is a user-token method, and a bot installed with
`always_online: false` shows as active for exactly as long as its socket is open, which is
this program's own lifetime and the one thing worth meaning.

The cost of the choice: `slack_sdk` is a dependency, pinned in `requirements.txt` and
installed by `install.sh` into the install's own virtualenv. Python's standard library has
no websocket client, and a Socket Mode connection cannot be held open without one. Its
*built-in* Socket Mode client is used rather than the aiohttp or websockets variants,
because that one implements the protocol itself and pulls in nothing further.
"""

